<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gissur Þorvaldsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1208–<a href="/years/1268">1268</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Gissur Thorvaldsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gissur Þorvaldsson was an Icelandic chieftain of the Haukdælir family and a leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sturlung-age">Sturlung Age</a>. He survived the burning of his farm at Flugumýri in 1253 and acted as an agent of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-iv-of-norway">Haakon IV of Norway</a>. After Iceland accepted Norwegian rule in 1262–1264, he became Iceland's only earl.</p></div>
